# ###Union##Generics#Built-in types
# TODO didn't understand Union
##Special attributes#Built-in types
# The implementation adds a few special read-only attributes to several object types, where they are
# relevant. Some of these are not reported by the dir() built-in function.
# - object.__dict__ : a dictionary or other mapping object used to store an object's (writable)
#   attributes.
# - instance.__class__ : the class to which a class instance belongs.
# - class.__bases__ : the tuple of base classes of a class object.
# - definition.__name__ : the name of the class, function, method, descriptor, or generator
#   instance.
# - definition.__qualname__  : the qualified name of the class, function, method, descriptor, or
#   generator instance.
# - class.__mro__ : this attribute is a tuple of classes that are considered when looking for base
#   classes during method resolution.
# - class.mro() : this method can be overridden by a metaclass to customize the method resolution
#   order for its instances. It is called at class instantiation, and its result is stored in
#   __mro__.
# - class.__subclasses__() : each class keeps a list of weak references to its immediate subclasses.
#   This method returns a list of all those references still alive. The list is in definition order.
#   Example:

# #Flow control
# ##for#Flow control
snippet fori for loop with i; note that i still exists after the loop ends
	for ${1:i} in range(${2:10}):
	    ${3:pass}

snippet forIndex for loop: iterate over a list by index; note that i still exists after the loop ends
	for ${1:i} in range(len(${2:list})):
	    ${3:pass}

snippet forMultiple for loop over multiple lists; the shortest list determines the length
	for ${1:loop variables} in zip(${2:lists to loop over}):
	    ${3:pass}

snippet forReversed for loop in reverse order
	for ${1:var} in reversed(${2:list}):
	    ${3:pass}

snippet forSorted for loop in sorted order
	for ${1:var} in sorted(${2:list}):
	    ${3:pass}

snippet forElse for loop that runs the else block when the loop finishes normally (no break, no exception)
	for ${1:for loop clause}:
	    ${2:pass}
	else:
	    ${3:pass}

snippet forEnumerate loop while also getting the index
	for ${2:i}, ${3:item} in enumerate(${1:list_var}):
	    ${4:pass}

